title: The Budget
subtitle: The Republic must pay for the year ahead.
tags: event
view-if: budget_due and not new_session and not finale and not game_ending
priority: 2
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_trade.svg
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetOpen(Q); !}

= The Budget of [+ bby +] BBY

The treasury holds **[+ treasury_txt +]**, and the Republic owes the InterGalactic Banking Clan **[+ debt_txt +]** ([+ debt_label +]). Trade along the hyperlanes is [+ trade_label +], which brings in about [+ bd_income_base +] before any new revenue. Running the Republic and its forces costs [+ bd_upkeep +], and interest comes to [+ bd_interest +].

[? if bd_write : The Caucus [? if rc_chancellor : holds the Chancellery?][? if not rc_chancellor : chairs the Finance & Commerce Committee?], so we write this year's budget. First: how will the Republic raise money? ?][? if not bd_write : The government proposes to [+ bd_gov_text +]. ?]

*A budget raises money one way and spends it on one priority. Any shortfall is lent by the Banking Clan, and every credit it lends buys the Muuns a little more influence over the Republic.*

- @rev_tariffs: Trade-route tariffs (about [+ bd_tariff_yield +]).
- @rev_levy: A levy on the Core worlds (3).
- @rev_loan: Borrow from the Banking Clan (3).
- @rev_bonds: Sell war bonds (about [+ bd_bond_yield +]).
- @rev_spice: Collect the spice duty (2).
- @rev_none: No new revenue: existing taxes only.
- @support: Support the government's budget.
- @oppose: Vote against it.
- @amend: Demand a different spending priority.

@rev_tariffs
view-if: bd_write
subtitle: Valorum's old policy. The guilds will be angry and may tighten their embargo; the Rim gains a little.
choose-if: date >= tariff_ban_until
unavailable-subtitle: We promised the guilds no new tariffs for now.
on-arrival: bd_rev = "tariffs"
go-to: priority

@rev_levy
view-if: bd_write
subtitle: Reliable. The Core worlds and the Moderates resent it, and our support in the Core dips.
on-arrival: bd_rev = "levy"
go-to: priority

@rev_loan
view-if: bd_write
subtitle: Painless now. The debt grows, and so does the Banking Clan's leverage.
on-arrival: bd_rev = "loan"
go-to: priority

@rev_bonds
view-if: bd_write and war
subtitle: What they raise depends on faith in the Republic. Buying them feels patriotic.
on-arrival: bd_rev = "bonds"
go-to: priority

@rev_spice
view-if: bd_write and spice_legal
subtitle: Easy money from the Kessel trade. Corruption grows.
on-arrival: bd_rev = "spice"
go-to: priority

@rev_none
view-if: bd_write
subtitle: No one is angered; the treasury will have to manage on trade and existing taxes.
on-arrival: bd_rev = "none"
go-to: priority

@support
view-if: not bd_write
subtitle: The government is grateful. [? if rc_in_govt : The coalition is calmer. ?]
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetApply(Q, Q.bd_gov_rev, Q.bd_gov_pri); Q[Q.chancellor_bloc + '_relation'] += 2; if (Q.rc_in_govt) Q.coalition_dissent -= 0.5; !}
go-to: budget_result

@oppose
view-if: not bd_write
subtitle: If it fails, a stopgap budget passes: no new revenue and no priorities. The government will not forgive it.
on-arrival: {!
var st = {};
for (var i = 0; i < Q.parties.length; i++) { var b = Q.parties[i]; st[b] = (Q.govt_blocs || []).indexOf(b) >= 0 ? 0.85 : 0.35; }
Q.bd_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 0);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('The government\'s budget', Q.bd_vote);
if (Q.bd_vote >= 50) { Q.bd_failed = 0; SW.budgetApply(Q, Q.bd_gov_rev, Q.bd_gov_pri); }
else { Q.bd_failed = 1; SW.budgetApply(Q, '', 'none'); Q.faith -= 0.5; Q.rc_momentum += 0.3; }
Q[Q.chancellor_bloc + '_relation'] -= 4;
if (Q.rc_in_govt) Q.coalition_dissent += 1;
!}
go-to: budget_result

@amend
view-if: not bd_write and rc_in_govt
subtitle: −1 political capital. We keep the government's revenue plan but choose what it pays for.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 1; Q.bd_rev = Q.bd_gov_rev; Q[Q.chancellor_bloc + '_relation'] -= 2; !}
go-to: priority

@priority
new-page: true

= What Will the Republic Pay For?

Choose one priority for the year. The treasury has [+ treasury_txt +], with upkeep of [+ bd_upkeep +] and interest of [+ bd_interest +] to cover; anything we cannot pay, the Banking Clan will lend.

- @pri_relief: Rim relief and hyperlane patrols (3).
- @pri_defence: Defence ([+ bd_defence_cost +]).
- @pri_subsidies: Subsidies for the Core and the guilds (2).
- @pri_repay: Repay the Banking Clan (3).
- @pri_none: Nothing new: balance the books.

@pri_relief
subtitle: Less hardship on the Rim, and safer, busier trade lanes.
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetApply(Q, Q.bd_rev, 'relief'); !}
go-to: budget_result

@pri_defence
subtitle: Stronger Judicial Forces. [? if war : The weakest front gets help. ?]Tibanna gas grows dearer.
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetApply(Q, Q.bd_rev, 'defence'); !}
go-to: budget_result

@pri_subsidies
subtitle: The Core Moderates and the guilds are pleased; corruption grows.
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetApply(Q, Q.bd_rev, 'subsidies'); !}
go-to: budget_result

@pri_repay
subtitle: The debt shrinks, and with it the Banking Clan's grip.
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetApply(Q, Q.bd_rev, 'repay'); !}
go-to: budget_result

@pri_none
subtitle: No new spending this year.
on-arrival: {! SW.budgetApply(Q, Q.bd_rev, 'none'); !}
go-to: budget_result

@budget_result
new-page: true

= The Budget Passes

[? if bd_failed : [+ vote_html +] The government's budget fails, and a stopgap measure keeps the Republic running: no new revenue, no new priorities. ?][? if not bd_failed : The Republic will raise money through **[+ bd_rev_name +]** and spend on **[+ bd_pri_name +]**. ?]

[+ bd_summary +]. [? if bd_borrowed > 0 : The Banking Clan lends the shortfall of [+ bd_borrowed +]. ?]

The treasury now holds [+ treasury_txt +], and the debt stands at [+ debt_txt +] ([+ debt_label +]).
